      a: 'Refresher runs box breathing free, with no session limit and no level gate. The round count and the infinite toggle are free too. Premium covers Builder and Wim Hof tuning, and keeps the coherent pace slider after your first five free sessions, following a 7-day trial.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Do Navy SEALs actually use box breathing?',
      a: 'The Cleveland Clinic describes box breathing as employed by the United States Navy SEALs. It gets used wherever someone needs a steady head under pressure, because a count of four is simple enough to hold when everything else is loud.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Is box breathing the same as square breathing?',
      a: 'Yes. Square breathing, four-square breathing, 4×4 breathing and equal breathing all name the same 4-4-4-4 pattern: four seconds in, four held, four out, four held. Refresher lists it as Box.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Is box breathing safe?',
      a: 'It is slow, gentle breathing with short holds. The Cleveland Clinic advises staying at a comfortable pace and not straining. Refresher is a timer for breathing and nothing more; if you have a heart or lung condition, ask your doctor before adding breath holds.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Does the box breathing pacer work on Apple Watch?',
      a: 'Yes. Refresher has its own Watch app. Once installed it runs the session on the wrist without the phone in reach, and it is the Watch that supplies the heart rate readings at the start and end. An iPhone has no heart rate sensor.',
    },
  ]}
  siblings={[
    { slug: '4-7-8-breathing-app', anchor: '4-7-8 breathing, the longest exhale of the fixed patterns' },
    { slug: 'coherent-breathing-app', anchor: 'Coherent breathing at 5.5 breaths per minute' },
    { slug: 'hrv-breathing-app', anchor: 'HRV breathing, and what the app will and will not show you' },
  ]}
  sources={[
    { url: 'https://health.clevelandclinic.org/box-breathing-benefits', supports: 'the alternative names, the Navy SEAL description, three to four rounds once or twice a day, and the advice not to strain' },
